  "preregistration": "ADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION of Family T's claimed T2MAP gain.\n\nSix independent checks, each a recomputed number rather than a reading of the family's\nown report. Writes artifacts/verify_family_t_adv/verification.json.\n\n  1 REPRODUCE   recompute the T2MAP candidate q arrays and the nested held-fold forecast\n                from scratch and score with harness.official.\n  2 NESTING     (a) structural: inner held partitions and their row weights lie strictly\n                inside each outer fold's fitting episodes;\n                (b) behavioural: corrupt bundle.truth on an outer fold's HELD episodes and\n                confirm the per-fold setting choice is bit-identical.\n  3 PROVENANCE  classify every file the family reads through scripts.stack_manifest.classify\n                and measure, numerically, what the protected r head's tail block is.\n  4 CAUSALITY   inject a fabricated 20x win AT the cutoff tick and a loss after it, and\n                separately invert every neighbour machine's whole pre-cutoff history, and\n                recompute T2MAP's q.\n  5 PAIRED      recompute harness.paired(arm, protected) from the saved submission CSV.\n  6 CONCAT      confirm the scored forecast is the concatenation of the four held folds,\n                each equal to its fold's chosen candidate, scored once over all 96 episodes.\n\nDeterminism: every reduction iterates sorted(...) or an index range.\n",
